+// ===================== root pre-search region instrumentation =====================
+// True while the root pre-search subtree is executing. pre_minimizer recurses into the REAL maximizer, so
+// the first-move-cutoff counters cannot otherwise tell the pre-search's own ordering from the main search's
+// -- the headline 87.55% FMC mixes tester and testee. A per-function test is impossible for the same reason;
+// only a call-region flag set around reorder_legal_moves can separate them.
+// g_fh_total/g_fh_first keep counting BOTH regions unchanged, so the existing line stays comparable and
+// main-only = total - pre is an arithmetic self-check.
+// Diagnostic instrumentation is COMPILE-TIME gated, not runtime gated. These counters are trivial to
+// execute but expensive to HAVE: reading the mutable g_in_presearch flag from inside the hot cutoff paths
+// costs ~30% of search speed under -Ofast -flto while leaving every decision byte-identical. Byte-identity
+// guards decisions, not cost -- so a runtime flag would not have caught this. Default builds stay clean;
+// build with -DCHESS_INSTRUMENT=1 (or flip this) only for a counter run, and never time such a build.
+#ifndef CHESS_INSTRUMENT
+#define CHESS_INSTRUMENT 0
+#endif
+
+static bool g_in_presearch = false;
+static long g_fh_first_pre = 0;
+static long g_fh_total_pre = 0;
